{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Thelen1966-fig6-edge-matched",
  "Source": "A. Thelen, \"Equivalent Layers in Multilayer Filters,\" J. Opt. Soc. Am. 56, 1533-1538 (1966). doi:10.1364/JOSA.56.001533 - Fig. 6 caption, p. 1536: 1.52 | 1.05[(H/2)L(H/2)]^3 [(H/2)L(H/2)]^12 | 1.0, nH = 2.3, nL = 1.56; text p. 1536, Eqs. (12)-(13)",
  "Notes": "Long-wave-pass edge filter matched to the substrate by a shifted (x1.05) equivalent layer repeated three times next to the substrate\nSpecification: Same stop band as the unmatched design, with reduced ripple in the long-wave pass band; matching by N_E1 = (N_E2 n_S)^1/2 and Gamma_E1 = (2v+1) 90 deg in the steep part of the equivalent-index curve.\nReported: Fig. 6 (p. 1536), %T vs lambda0/lambda 0.6-1.2 (read from plot, approximate): T ~ 0 from about 0.88 to 1.12; pass band (lambda0/lambda < ~0.87) stays at roughly 95-100 % with small ripple, versus large dips for the unmatched design. Fig. 10 (p. 1538): the Fig. 6 design built with TiO2/Si2O3 on 1.52 plate glass gives an edge (T rising from ~0 to ~90 %) near 640-655 nm and ~90-95 % T from 660 to 800 nm; lambda0 not stated. Total optical thickness 12 x 2 QW + 3 x 1.05 x 2 QW = 30.3 QW.\nNotes: Paper lists substrate first; reversed here so layer 1 is next to air: 12 normal periods on the air side, then the three 1.05-scaled periods next to the substrate. The caption prints '1.05[(h/2)L(H/2)]^3' with a lowercase h, taken as a typo for H. The 1.05 factor multiplies every layer in those three periods (H/2 -> 0.525 QW, L -> 1.05 QW). Adjacent H halves merged: the junction layer is 0.5 + 0.525 = 1.025 QW H. 45 printed sub-layers -> 31 layers. reference_nm = 1000 arbitrary (lambda0 not given); normal incidence assumed. Text: the shifted layer had to be repeated three times to meet Eq. (13); no match between the multilayer and air was needed.\nLayers from Fig. 6 caption, p. 1536: 1.52 | 1.05[(H/2)L(H/2)]^3 [(H/2)L(H/2)]^12 | 1.0, nH = 2.3, nL = 1.56; text p. 1536, Eqs. (12)-(13); layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), compare with the paper: ours T < 1 % from 0.886 to 1.117; pass band 0.70-0.86 between 56.4 % and 99.9 %; paper stop band 0.88-1.12; pass band 95-100 % (read from Fig. 6).",
